{% extends 'help/_layout.html.twig' %}
{% block help_title %}Settings &amp; Notifications{% endblock %}

{% block help_body %}
<figure class="figure d-block border rounded shadow-sm overflow-hidden mb-4 w-100">
    <img src="{{ asset('images/help/settings.png') }}" class="figure-img img-fluid mb-0 w-100"
         alt="The Settings hub — cards grouped into Preferences, Notifications, Security & API, Billing, and Account">
</figure>
<p>Settings is where you control how NouriLoop reaches you, how it displays your data, and how it sounds.
Open it from the account menu (your name, top right) — everything lives on one hub page, grouped into a few
cards.</p>

<h2 class="h5 fw-bold mt-4">Preferences</h2>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Timezone</strong> — sets what counts as "today" for your dashboard and when your evening
    digest goes out. If your device's local time ever disagrees with this setting (say, after a move),
    NouriLoop shows a one-click banner offering to fix it.</li>
    <li><strong>Units</strong> — metric or imperial: weight in kilograms or pounds, and blood glucose in
    mmol/L or mg/dL.</li>
    <li><strong>Language</strong> — NouriLoop speaks six languages — English, Spanish, German, French,
    Russian, and Hindi — with regional options for English and Spanish. Your choice also applies to the
    reminder and check-in emails NouriLoop sends you.</li>
    <li><strong>GLP-1 mode</strong> — an optional mode for people taking a GLP-1 medication: extra focus on
    protein, gentler portion guidance, and insights into possible nausea triggers.</li>
    <li><strong>Voice &amp; tone</strong> — three sliders that tune how NouriLoop's AI coaching notes sound,
    from strictly businesslike to warm and playful. Style only — the numbers and advice never change.</li>
</ul>

<h2 class="h5 fw-bold mt-4">Notifications</h2>
<p>NouriLoop can send you a daily digest covering things worth a glance — no meals logged, health data going
stale, calories out of your usual range, or nutrient gaps. To receive them:</p>
<ol>
    <li>Turn on the notice types you want (they're all off by default).</li>
    <li>Choose a delivery channel: <strong>Email</strong>, <strong>SMS</strong>, or <strong>Both</strong>.</li>
    <li>For text messages, add your phone number (in <code>+1…</code> format) and tick the SMS consent
    box. Text-message delivery is part of the paid plans — the daily digest by text starts with
    <strong>Loop</strong>, and goal check-ins delivered by email or text come with
    <strong>Loop+</strong>.</li>
</ol>
<p class="text-muted small">Everything also appears in the in-app notification bell, on every plan. This page
is also where you can bring back the "Get set up" checklist if you dismissed it before finishing.</p>

<h2 class="h5 fw-bold mt-4">API tokens</h2>
<p>Create an <strong>API token</strong> to sync health data automatically from a script or an app like Health
Auto Export. Each token is shown once when you create it, and you can revoke it anytime. See
<a href="{{ path('app_help_show', {topic: 'health-metrics'}) }}">Importing Health Data</a> and
<a href="{{ path('app_help_show', {topic: 'connect-cgm'}) }}">Connect Your CGM</a>.</p>

<h2 class="h5 fw-bold mt-4">Subscription</h2>
<p>See which plan you're on and what it includes. Upgrading takes you through a secure checkout; existing
subscribers can update their payment method, switch plans, or cancel anytime through the
<strong>Manage subscription</strong> button — access always continues to the end of the period you've paid
for.</p>

<h2 class="h5 fw-bold mt-4">Account</h2>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Start fresh</strong> — erases your logged data (meals, health readings, symptoms, goals) but
    keeps your account, settings, and subscription, so you can begin again with a clean slate.</li>
    <li><strong>Delete my account</strong> — schedules your account and all its data for permanent deletion
    after a 30-day grace period. Any subscription is cancelled right away, and you can change your mind
    anytime during those 30 days with one click.</li>
</ul>
{% endblock %}

